module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.typed_snapshot_serializes_shared_structure_by_value

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data typed_snapshot_serializes_shared_structure_by_value: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "typed_snapshot_serializes_shared_structure_by_value" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a per-module typed snapshot serializes, BY VALUE, structure that is shared in memory across modules. TypeEnv holds symbol_index, intern_table and source_indices, which are per-reconcile or pool-scoped and byte-identical across modules, plus its parent environments, all behind Rc and all derived serde::Serialize. serde writes an Rc by value, so ONE module's snapshot re-serializes every pool-scoped field in every environment it reaches, and decode rebuilds each as a separate, unshared copy. It is the identity-rewire class (name_canonicalisation_depends_on_the_co_compiled_graph, removed by gunbc#13076): structural sharing lost at a copy boundary, here serialization.",
    "HARM: snapshot size scales with (environments reachable from the module) x (size of the pool-scoped fields), independent of the module's own content. A one-item module encoded as a multi-GB entry, a 47-module entry encoded hundreds of GB of throughput cold, and a warm decode materialized many GB of unshared copies that the process then retained.",
    "SPECIMEN AND MEASUREMENT (calm-pike-525 with neat-boar-16, srv1, 2026-10-03). Instruments: the probes on branches calm-pike-525/warm-route-residency-probe (heap residency and typed-store counters), calm-pike-525/snapshot-grain-probe (per-module encoded bytes against reachable environments: near-linear, independent of item count) and calm-pike-525/snapshot-field-probe (per-field bytes: symbol_index dominates, identical across modules; the module's own fields are KB-sized). Figures are in those runs' logs. The analysis is in docs/plans/type-env-single-authority-design.md.",
    "DISPOSITION: the persisted side is FIXED by deletion. gunbc#13064 deleted PersistentTypedStore (GUNBC_TYPED_STORE_PERSIST) as a regression writing GBs per entry; that cost is this class. The same encoder survives in the in-memory cross-worker store (shared_typecheck_store encode_typed_snapshot / decode_typed_snapshot). On main it is armed only in a cfg(test) module and in required_floor_runner run_discovery_corpus_with_options_inner, whose sole entry run_discovery_corpus_with_options has a unit test as its only caller. No production route encodes a typed snapshot, so no consumer demands the cross-worker share at CI's floor width (DESIGN 2's demand-first rule), and no repair was built (calm-boar-904 ruling, 2026-10-03).",
    "UPDATE (2026-10-04): the in-memory cross-worker store is DELETED too. Its arming path, the discovery-corpus width machinery, was deleted as unreachable first; SharedTypecheckCaches, build_multi_entry_index_with_shared_caches, the MultiEntryIndex cross_worker_store field and v1_compiler.shared_typecheck_store itself followed as test-only. NO LIVE INSTANCE REMAINS: nothing in the seed serializes a TypecheckModuleResult, and the per-index typed_module_cache holds Rc values whose sharing is intact. The class is now a design hazard for the next producer, not a live defect. The DISPOSITION and RUNG paragraphs here are superseded by this entry for the in-memory store; the next-rung trigger is unchanged.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the serialized type has an Rc field whose referent is shared across the values being serialized independently, AND that referent is large relative to the value's own content. A field that is genuinely per-value is not this class.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: silent -- found by attributing a warm-route memory delta, not by any check. RUNG NOW: mitigatable -- no production route reaches the encoder, so the harm is not reachable, but the encoder still writes by value and nothing refuses a new caller. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- a snapshot format that names pool-scoped fields by a content-complete pool key (a content hash of the pooled fields' canonical bytes), carries parents by module identity, and refuses on an absent or mismatched pool record. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: any production consumer that demands cross-worker or cross-process typed-snapshot sharing. That demand is the trigger to build the pool-keyed format before it is armed, under the conditions in calm-boar-904's 2026-10-03 ruling (one pool record per pool identity, typed refusal on absent/stale/mismatch, a format-version bump, and controls: lookup equality with a fresh compile, one shared decoded symbol_index per pool, mismatch refusal, measured per-module bytes).",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
